<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov gold imports down 56.3 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov gold imports down 56.3 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in November plunged by 56.3 percent from a year earlier to 6.43 tonnes, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   Nov 96    Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		   6.43	6.91	  14.71</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	     1.13	0.85	   5.44</p>
<p> South Africa	  1.05	1.58	   1.10</p>
<p> Britain		 0.51	1.00	   1.60</p>
<p> Canada		  0.50	0.50	   0.17</p>
<p> South Korea	   0.03	0.30	   0.60</p>
<p> Switzerland	   0.40	0.59	   3.21</p>
<p>Gold imports in the first 11 months of 1996 totalled 126.30 tonnes, against 249.67 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 7431)</p>
</text>
